<Page title={`About ${site.BRAND}: Who We Are and How This Site Works`} description={`${site.BRAND} publishes free, practical guides on this topic: real numbers, real sources, and tools that replace guesswork instead of filler.`}>
  <p>{site.BRAND} is an independent site. {site.author.bio}</p>

  <h2>What this site is</h2>
  <p>Dog training advice online is mostly recycled. This site is built around drills you can run in a driveway or a hallway: step counts, repetition targets, and the specific cue timing that separates a dog who sits on command from one who sits when it feels like it. Recall, leash pulling, and crate training each get their own drill sequence rather than a single "obedience" checklist.</p>

  <h2>How we work</h2>
  <p>Our drills are built from certified trainer methodology and behavior science on operant conditioning, then run with real dogs before they're published. Guides are drafted with AI assistance and checked against that methodology before going live, which our <a href="/editorial/">editorial policy</a> explains. If a drill doesn't work as written after testing, we rewrite it instead of leaving it up.</p>

  <h2>How we make money</h2>
  <p>Every drill and guide is free. The site earns affiliate commissions when readers buy training tools, treats, or courses through links here. Full terms are in our <a href="/disclosure/">disclosure</a>.</p>

  <h2>Corrections</h2>
  <p>If a drill isn't working for your dog or a step seems wrong, tell us through the <a href="/contact/">contact form</a>. We revise and date the change.</p>
</Page>
